# Being in the [[centre]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1814|author=w:William Wordsworth|chapter=The Parsonage|title=The Poetical Works of William Wordsworth|volume=V|location=London|publisher=Longman|year_published=1827|page=340|pageurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=sY5LAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA340|passage=Egyption Thebes; / Tyre by the margin of the sounding waves; / Palmyra, '''central''' in the Desert, fell; / And the Arts died by which they had been raised.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-27|volume=408|issue=8846|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21582242-robotic-model-what-plants-get-up-under-surface-putting-down-roots Putting down roots]
|passage=The plantoid{{...}}will have a '''central''' stem containing a reservoir of liquid plastic of a sort that can be frozen by ultraviolet light. Half a dozen cylindrical roots will branch off this stem, and the plastic will flow through these from the reservoir to the tip. As in a real root, the tip will be a specialised structure.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=The internet is in decline – it needs rewilding
|author=John Naughton
|date=2024-05-04|magazine=w:The Guardian
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/may/04/the-internet-is-in-decline-it-needs-rewilding
|passage=The network had no '''central''' ownership or controller; and it did only one thing – transfer data packets from one edge of the network to their destination at another edge.
}}
# Having or containing the centre of something.
# Being very important, or key to something.
#: {{synonyms|en|dominant|main|principal}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 7, 2012|author=Phil McNulty|work=BBC Sport
|title=[http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/19460608 Moldova 0-5 England]
|passage=Cleverley was a '''central''' figure as England took the lead inside three minutes. He saw his shot handled by Moldovan defender Simion Bulgaru and Lampard drilled home the penalty in trademark fashion.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 May 6|author=Jim Steer|title=Full Business Case offers fresh insight into HS2's prospects|journal=Rail|page=51, photo caption|text=Passengers crowd in the main concourse at London [[Euston]] on January 28 2017, before boarding West Coast Main Line services. The urgent need to relieve congestion and improve reliability on the [[WCML]] remains '''central''' in the recently published Full Business Case for HS2.}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} Exerting its action towards the peripheral organs.
# {{lb|en|algebra}} Belong or relating to the [[center]] of an [[algebraic structure]].
